vulkan: refuse to write a VK_NULL_HANDLE imageView into a descriptor set

A VK_NULL_HANDLE imageView reaching vkCmdPushDescriptorSetKHR is a
process-fatal SIGSEGV on the NVIDIA proprietary driver (measured on
610.43.03, crash offset 0xf8a1b5, si_addr=0xf0): the driver NULL-checks
the sampler but dereferences the view unconditionally. Observed three
times from scale_vulkan's ff_vk_filter_process_simple ->
ff_vk_shader_update_img_array path under VRAM/resource churn, where a
view that passed ff_vk_create_imageviews' RET-checked creation
nevertheless arrived NULL at the descriptor write (bd remora-7ps,
remora-fi8c).

Skipping the write loses at worst one frame's sampling correctness for
that binding; pushing it loses the process. Callers of the array helper
ignore per-plane failures, so a skip degrades instead of aborting the
filter chain.

--- a/libavutil/vulkan.c
+++ b/libavutil/vulkan.c
@@ -2706,6 +2706,13 @@ int ff_vk_shader_update_img(FFVulkanContext *s, FFVkExecContext *e,
 {
     FFVulkanDescriptorSet *desc_set = &shd->desc_set[set];

+    if (view == VK_NULL_HANDLE) {
+        av_log(s, AV_LOG_WARNING, "Refusing descriptor write of a VK_NULL_HANDLE "
+               "imageView (set %i binding %i elem %i) — skipping, output may be "
+               "wrong for this frame\n", set, bind, offs);
+        return AVERROR(EINVAL);
+    }
+
     VkDescriptorImageInfo desc_pool_write_info_img = {
         .sampler = sampler,
         .imageView = view,
